    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/all_jobs.atom": {
      "title": "University of Central Arkansas: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:jobs.uca.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs University of Central Arkansas: All Jobs 2026-08-27T08:50:33-05:00 https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19675 2026-08-27T08:50:33-05:00 2026-08-27T08:50:33-05:00 Research Compliance Officer <div>The RCO oversees all aspects of research compliance in the areas of human subject protection, animal care and use, financial conflicts of interest, export control, and the responsible conduct of research, and supports the Research Integrity Officer in matters involving allegations of noncompliance or research misconduct. The RCO serves as the Institutional Review Board administrator, the Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee administrator, and the university's Export Control Officer. The RCO establishes and maintains working relationships with individuals at all levels of the institution's research community, educates the UCA community on the policies and procedures governing the review of research, and keeps current on the regulatory landscape through professional development, including regional and national conferences.</div> 441000 - Research Compliance https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19418 2026-07-14T11:18:56-05:00 2026-08-21T16:40:25-05:00 CLASS Third Party Verification Field Observer <div>The Arkansas Research Center (ARC) at the University of Central Arkansas is seeking twelve full-time Regional CLASS Observers to conduct independent observations as part of its statewide CLASS Third-Party Observation Verification project, conducted on behalf of the Arkansas Department of Education, Office of Early Childhood. ARC has been engaged to conduct verification observations across all 75 Arkansas counties.<br><br></div><div>Observers are organized into six geographic service areas, with two observers assigned to each region. Candidates must indicate their preferred region at the time of application and must reside in that region. Positions vary in county coverage and travel demand:</div><ul><li><strong>Northwest:</strong> Covers 3 counties — Benton, Carroll, and Washington.</li><li><strong>North/Ozarks:</strong> Covers 18 counties across the Ozark region, from Faulkner and Pope counties north through Baxter, Boone, and Newton.</li><li><strong>Northeast:</strong> Covers 10 counties across the northeastern Delta and river corridor, including Craighead, Crittenden, and Mississippi counties.</li><li><strong>Central:</strong> Covers Pulaski and Saline counties.</li><li><strong>West/River Valley:</strong> Covers 23 counties across western and south-central Arkansas.</li><li><strong>South/Delta:</strong> Covers 19 counties across the southern Delta, from Jefferson and Lonoke counties south through Ashley, Chicot, and Union.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Qualified candidates will hold active Teachstone CLASS Observer certification for both the Infant-Toddler 2.0 and Pre-K 2.0 tools and bring a minimum of five years of experience in early childhood education or a closely related field, including at least three years of direct professional experience in 0–5 classroom settings. Candidates may not hold existing coaching, professional development, or supervisory relationships with early childhood programs in their preferred regional service area.<br><br>This position is currently funded by the Arkansas Department of Education, Office of Early Childhood, for July 1 through December 15 due to federal funding limitations. ADE-OEC will determine additional funding in the fall; the full twelve-month salary would be $75,000.</div> 320000 - Dean-College of Education https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/18773 2026-04-02T18:30:00-05:00 2026-04-02T18:30:00-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The University of Central Arkansas Assistant or Associate Professor is responsible for teaching, research and service. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. The position is tenure track and a nine-month appointment.</div> 348000 - Dept of Comm Science & Disorders https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19700 2026-09-02T08:53:49-05:00 2026-09-02T08:53:49-05:00 Associate Director of Cooperative Education Program <ul><li>Maintain employer relationships and recruit and/or develop new internship opportunities/programs to support experiential learning and student development.</li><li>Responsible for implementing office marketing plan for students, faculty, and staff.</li><li>Supervise professional staff.</li><li>Report to Executive Director of Career Services.</li></ul> 603500 - Cooperative Education Program https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19615 2026-08-20T09:59:41-05:00 2026-08-20T09:59:41-05:00 Visiting Lecturer of Interior Design <div>The Department of Art and Design at the University of Central Arkansas invites applications for a full-time Visiting Assistant Professor or Visiting Lecturer I position in the Interior Design Program beginning January 2, 2027.<br><br>The department seeks a candidate whose teaching and professional interests connect historical precedent, preservation research, and contemporary interior design practice. In addition to teaching responsibilities, this position will serve as Curriculum and NCPE Coordinator, supporting the Interior Design Program&amp;#39;s National Council for Preservation Education (NCPE) Certificate of Proficiency and assisting with curriculum assessment, course coordination, accreditation support, and continuous improvement initiatives.<br><br>The successful candidate will support the programs initiatives in historic preservation, sustainability, accreditation, interdisciplinary collaboration, study abroad, and professional<br>preparation. The position will also serve as a strong advocate for the Interior Design Program through collaboration with students, faculty, alumni, advisory board members, professional<br>organizations, and industry partners.<br><br>This is a nine-month faculty appointment with an expected teaching load of twelve credit hours per<br>semester.</div> 331000 - Art https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19013 2026-04-30T13:25:23-05:00 2026-04-30T13:25:23-05:00 Clinical Instructor I <div>The University of Central Arkansas Clinical Instructor I is responsible for teaching, research and service. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. The position is non-tenure track and a nine-month appointment.</div> 347000 - Psychology & Counseling https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19655 2026-08-26T10:27:00-05:00 2026-08-26T10:27:00-05:00 Clinical Instructor I <div>The University of Central Arkansas Clinical Instructor I is responsible for teaching, research and service. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. The position is non-tenure track and a nine-month appointment.</div> 348000 - Dept of Comm Science & Disorders https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19195 2026-06-01T14:07:36-05:00 2026-06-01T14:07:36-05:00 Adjunct Instructor of Music - Collaborative Piano <div>The University of Central Arkansas is searching for an Adjunct <strong>Collaborative Pianist</strong>. The faculty member is responsible for serving as accompanist for ensembles, recitals, degree recitals, faculty recitals, guest artist recitals, and instruction as needed. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. The position is adjunct.<br><br>The Department of Music in the College of the Arts Humanities and Social Sciences enjoys endowments and private scholarship funds of approximately $2 million, annual university performance scholarships of over $850,000, a visiting artist series, and NASM accreditation. Many performances are presented in the state-of-the-art, 1100+-seat, Donald W. Reynolds Performance Hall and the new Windgate Center for the Fine and Performing Arts, a 100,000 sq ft arts space in the heart of the campus, home to Music Art, and Theatre. The department serves 250+ majors and minors, and offers both undergraduate and graduate degrees: BA, BM (Music Education, Composition, Performance, Piano Pedagogy, and Jazz and Studio Music), MM (Music Education, Performance, Conducting, Theory), as well as a Graduate Performance Certificate program. The faculty is composed of no fewer than 33 full-time and approximately 18 adjunct members, most of whom have national and international reputations.<br><br></div> 335000 - Music https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19699 2026-09-02T08:15:37-05:00 2026-09-02T08:15:38-05:00 HVAC Specialist <div>The HVAC Specialist provides HVAC services on campus, with a specific responsibility to identify repair and/or replacement needs, perform installations, maintenance, and upgrades of HVAC systems and equipment, and assists other skilled trades in the Physical Plant. Other duties as assigned.</div> 550000 - Office-Physical Plant https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19590 2026-08-18T07:22:40-05:00 2026-08-18T07:22:41-05:00 Pre-BSN Student Coordinator <div>The Pre-BSN Student Coordinator is to assist students in their growth and development by constructing meaningful educational plans which are compatible with their life goals. It is a continuous and consistent process which is built upon the basis of frequent, accumulated personal contacts between advisor and advisee. The Pre-BSN Student Coordinator is responsible for assessing, and counseling individuals and providing individual/group education and vocational guidance services. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy.</div> 344000 - Nursing https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/18783 2026-04-02T18:31:07-05:00 2026-04-02T18:31:08-05:00 Assistant Professor - School of Nursing <div>The University of Central Arkansas (UCA) is seeking a <strong>full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor (9-month appointment)</strong> to join the School of Nursing. This on-campus role is designed for a doctorally prepared (DNP or PhD) Family Nurse Practitioner who will shape the next generation of nursing professionals. The successful candidate will lead innovative educational programs, conduct scholarly research, and contribute to a supportive, inclusive academic environment. Learn more at: <a href=\"http://www.uca.edu/nursing\"><strong>www.uca.edu/nursing</strong></a></div> 344000 - Nursing https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19710 2026-09-04T14:11:11-05:00 2026-09-04T14:11:11-05:00 Fiscal Support Analyst <div>The Fiscal Support Analyst is responsible for performing a wide variety of fiscal related tasks that are standard or regular support duties within an assigned department or program and for researching financial data and preparing reports. This position is governed by Generally Accepted Accounting Principles, state and federal laws, and agency/institution policy.<br>Apply at jobs.uca.edu.</div> 335000 - Music https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19633 2026-08-24T07:26:12-05:00 2026-08-24T07:26:12-05:00 Food Preparation Supervisor/Cook <div>The Food Preparation Supervisor (Cook) is responsible for meal preparation, supervision of part-time servers, directing food service activities in the absence of the Food Service Director, monitoring security and safety practices, coordinating the production and serving of food. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy.</div> 755000 - College Square Retirement Ctr https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19016 2026-04-30T13:36:57-05:00 2026-04-30T13:36:57-05:00 Assistant Professor - School of Nursing <div>The University of Central Arkansas (UCA) is seeking a <strong>full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor (9-month appointment)</strong> to join the School of Nursing. This on-campus role is designed for a doctorally prepared (DNP or PhD) Family Nurse Practitioner who will shape the next generation of nursing professionals. The successful candidate will lead innovative educational programs, conduct scholarly research, and contribute to a supportive, inclusive academic environment. Learn more at: <a href=\"http://www.uca.edu/nursing\"><strong>www.uca.edu/nursing</strong></a></div> 344000 - Nursing"
    },
