    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19655": {
      "title": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Clinical Instructor I",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Clinical Instructor I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW   Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Instructor I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit the following materials electronically through the University of Central Arkansas employment portal at https://jobs.uca.edu/: A letter of interest describing qualifications for the position; A current résumé or curriculum vitae; A statement of teaching philosophy that addresses the applicant's approach to student learning, mentorship, and clinical education, as applicable; and Contact information for three professional references, including each reference's name, title, institution or organization, email address, and telephone number. Only complete applications will receive full consideration. Questions regarding the position or the application process should be directed to the Chair of the Search Committee: Candice Robinson; email: crobinson@uca.edu; phone: (501) 450-5776. Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0382026 Working Title Clinical Instructor I Department Org 348000 - Dept of Comm Science & Disorders Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The University of Central Arkansas Clinical Instructor I is responsible for teaching, research and service. This position is governed by state and federal laws and agency/institution policy. The position is non-tenure track and a nine-month appointment. Job Duties and Responsibilities The successful candidate will provide high-quality classroom instruction and clinical education to undergraduate and graduate students within the Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders. Teaching responsibilities may include undergraduate foundational courses. Clinical responsibilities will include supervising and mentoring graduate student clinicians in the University Speech-Language-Hearing Center, while providing evidence-based assessment and intervention services across a broad range of communication disorders. The successful candidate will foster students’ clinical reasoning, professionalism, and development of competencies required for entry into professional practice. Additional responsibilities include collaborating with faculty to strengthen academic and clinical programming, supporting the growth and enhancement of clinical services, participating in departmental, college, and university service activities, and contributing to student recruitment, retention, and program initiatives. Candidates with experience in interprofessional education and collaborative practice, clinical innovation, and community engagement are preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities This position requires knowledge and skills to serve a wide variety of disorders in addition to working closely with graduate students and faculty in the clinical process. Interprofessional collaborative practices experience preferred. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience Master’s degree in Speech-Language Pathology Preferred Education and/or Experience Minimum of 5 years of clinical experience in a variety of settings (pediatrics, school, rehab), experience with telehealth, andexperience supervising master’s level clinical students. License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) Required: ASHA Certification – current CCC - SLP Current ABESPA licensure or eligibility for ABESPA licensure. University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 09/01/2026 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 08/25/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit the following materials electronically through the University of Central Arkansas employment portal at https://jobs.uca.edu/: A letter of interest describing qualifications for the position; A current résumé or curriculum vitae; A statement of teaching philosophy that addresses the applicant’s approach to student learning, mentorship, and clinical education, as applicable; and Contact information for three professional references, including each reference’s name, title, institution or organization, email address, and telephone number. Only complete applications will receive full consideration. Questions regarding the position or the application process should be directed to the Chair of the Search Committee: Candice Robinson; email: crobinson@uca.edu; phone: (501) 450-5776. Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts License or Certification Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae Other Transcripts Veteran's Documents Additional Documents University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uca.edu/bookmarks?posting_id=19655": {
      "title": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Log In Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW   Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Your session has expired. Please log in. Log in to your account Required fields are indicated with an asterisk * * Username * Password Forgot your username or password? Current Employee Log In Or Create an Account × The Chronicle of Higher Education had retired the \"Apply with Vitae\" login option. No need to worry, read on for steps to access your account. To access the account, return to the login page using the \"X\" in the upper corner or clicking outside of this pop-up box. Use the \"Forgot your username or password?\" link with your original Chronicle Vitae username to create a new password and access your account. University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uca.edu/postings/19615": {
      "title": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Visiting Lecturer of Interior Design",
      "description": "University of Central Arkansas Employment Opportunities | Visiting Lecturer of Interior Design Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NEW   Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Visiting Lecturer of Interior Design Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Requesting the following as part of application submittal: -3 Letters of Recommendation Position Details Position Information Posting Number F0372026 Working Title Visiting Lecturer of Interior Design Department Org 331000 - Art Why should you work at UCA? We are excited that you are considering joining the UCA Family—the faculty, staff, students and alumni—who make the University of Central Arkansas a great place to work! At the University of Central Arkansas, we value our employees striving to maintain a work-life balance. We realize that this affects the overall well-being of employees while learning to prioritize challenging work and the ability to make a difference. Participation in university-wide flexible work schedules may be available for certain positions. Training is provided on systems or job-specific software, and tools are available supporting professional and personal development. The benefits package allows you to customize your benefits to meet your current needs, with the ability to adjust them as your priorities change. This includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, 80% tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a retirement program with university contributions of 10% of employee salary. Also available are health and wellness incentives, as well as access to sports and cultural activities on campus for the family, free gym membership and equipment rentals. Position Summary The Department of Art and Design at the University of Central Arkansas invites applications for a full-time Visiting Assistant Professor or Visiting Lecturer I position in the Interior Design Program beginning January 2, 2027. The department seeks a candidate whose teaching and professional interests connect historical precedent, preservation research, and contemporary interior design practice. In addition to teaching responsibilities, this position will serve as Curriculum and NCPE Coordinator, supporting the Interior Design Program&#39;s National Council for Preservation Education ( NCPE ) Certificate of Proficiency and assisting with curriculum assessment, course coordination, accreditation support, and continuous improvement initiatives. The successful candidate will support the programs initiatives in historic preservation, sustainability, accreditation, interdisciplinary collaboration, study abroad, and professional preparation. The position will also serve as a strong advocate for the Interior Design Program through collaboration with students, faculty, alumni, advisory board members, professional organizations, and industry partners. This is a nine-month faculty appointment with an expected teaching load of twelve credit hours per semester. Job Duties and Responsibilities Teach undergraduate courses in design history, architectural history, historic preservation, and related subject areas. Teach assigned Art Foundations coursework as needed by the department. Serve as Curriculum and NCPE Coordinator for the Interior Design Program. Maintain student records and documentation associated with the National Council for Preservation Education ( NCPE ) Certificate of Proficiency. Assist with coordination, assessment, and continuous improvement of the preservation curriculum. Work closely with the Program Director to maintain curriculum maps, course sequencing documentation, assessment records, curriculum databases, and course cohesion across the curriculum. This position will serve on the Art & Design Curriculum committee. Support course coordination and curricular cohesion across the Interior Design Program. Participate in curriculum assessment, accreditation documentation, and continuous improvement activities associated with CIDA , NASAD , NCPE , and university requirements. Support study abroad initiatives, experiential learning opportunities, and community-engaged preservation projects. Advise and mentor undergraduate students. Participate in recruitment, retention, and student success initiatives. Serve as a strong advocate for the Interior Design Program and its students. Collaborate with industry partners, alumni, advisory board members, and community stakeholders to advance program initiatives. Participate in departmental, college, university, and program-area meetings and committees. Collaborate with faculty across Interior Design, Studio Art, Art Education, and related disciplines. Maintain active professional engagement and contribute to the advancement of the discipline through professional practice, scholarship, or service. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated expertise in architectural history, interiors history, historic preservation, preservation research, or closely related subject matter. Evidence of successful teaching, scholarship, professional practice, or a combination thereof. The successful candidate will contribute to a nationally accredited interior design program through teaching, service, student mentorship, and professional engagement. Primary responsibilities include teaching History of Architecture, Interiors, and Furnishings I; History of Architecture, Interiors, and Furnishings II; Historic Research for Interior Preservation; and selected Art Foundations courses such as 2D Design, 3D Design, Drawing, or Fabrication based on departmental needs and candidate qualifications. Skills Considered Essential for Success -Knowledge of the organization and administration of higher education. -Knowledge of state, federal, and university rules, regulations and procedures. -Ability to work in a diverse and dynamic environment. -Ability to work collaboratively and independently with common goals as a part of a team. -Ability to make sound judgments. -Effective interpersonal communication, writing, and organizational abilities. -Civility in all interactions. -Demonstrate effective follow-up. Required Education and/or Experience Master’s degree in Interior Design, Interior Architecture, Architecture, Historic Preservation, Architectural History, Art History, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. NCIDQ certification or ability to obtain NCIDQ certification within one year of appointment. For Visiting Assistant Professor: Earned doctorate (PhD, DDes, EdD, or equivalent terminal degree) in Interior Design, Interior Architecture, Architecture, Historic Preservation, Architectural History, Art History, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. NCIDQ certification or ability to obtain NCIDQ certification within one year of appointment. Preferred Education and/or Experience Terminal Degree and NCIDQ Certificate License(s)/Certifications (Required or Preferred) LEED and/or WELL Certification in addition to professional membership in ASID , IIDA , AIA or similar organization University, Campus, and Community Description Thank you for your interest in employment at the University of Central Arkansas. Founded in 1907, UCA has an enrollment of more than 10,000 students and employs over 1,300 full-time employees. The university offers more than 85 undergraduate and 59 graduate certificate and degree programs, including doctoral programs in five disciplines. UCA is proud of its tradition of teaching excellence and its contributions in research, scholarship, and creative activities. Desired start date 01/04/2027 Will this position be Onsite, Remote, or Hybrid? Onsite Posting Detail Information Background Check Statement This position may be subject to a pre-employment criminal, sex-offender registry, financial history background check and drug screening. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication and/or adverse financial history alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background checks and drug screening information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. UCA EEO Statement The University of Central Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. In keeping with its nondiscrimination policy in employment, admissions and other functions and programs, the university considers employees and students on the basis of individual merit and will not discriminate against a person on the basis of gender, race or color, ethnicity, religion, spiritual beliefs, national origin, age, familial status, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, disability, political beliefs, intellectual perspective, genetic information, military status, or other factors irrelevant to participation in its programs. Open Date 08/18/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Requesting the following as part of application submittal: -3 Letters of Recommendation Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Additional Documents Teaching Philosophy License or Certification Veteran's Documents Writing Sample Other Transcripts Other Document Portfolio / Supplemental Materials University of Central Arkansas Human Resources 201 Donaghey Ave. Wingo Hall Conway, AR 72035 1.501.450.3181 1.501.450.5088 (fax) humanresources@uca.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
